# An assignment pattern given as an instance's parameter value takes its
# type from the instantiated module's parameter.  When that module is not
# read yet, the error now says so in hierarchy's words (2026-10-31; the
# conformance ladder read OpenTitan otp_ctrl.sv, `otp_ctrl_lci #(.Info(...))`,
# before otp_ctrl_lci and only saw "could not be resolved", so it never
# loaded the child).
logger -expect error "Module `leaf' referenced in module `top' is not part of the design .the assignment pattern given for its parameter Info" 1
read_verilog -sv <<EOF
package pp;
  typedef struct packed { logic [3:0] off; logic sec; } info_t;
endpackage
module top import pp::*; (output [3:0] o, output s);
  leaf #(.Info('{off: 4'd9, sec: 1'b0})) u (.o(o), .s(s));
endmodule
EOF
